---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About Tim - Dad Investor" 
  description="I help Financial DIYers own their money and future through plain-English education and simple financial tools."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="bg-[#F8FAFC] pt-16 pb-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b border-slate-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center space-y-8">
      
      <!-- Headline -->
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold text-[#0F172A] tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Hi— I'm Tim. I help Financial DIYers own their money and future.
      </h1>

      <!-- Centered Circular Avatar with Accent Ring -->
      <div class="relative inline-block mt-4">
        <div class="w-40 h-40 sm:w-48 sm:h-48 rounded-full overflow-hidden border-4 border-[#10B981] shadow-lg mx-auto bg-slate-100">
          <Image 
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534528741775-53994a69daeb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&q=80" 
            alt="Tim Ellis" 
            width={400} 
            height={400}
            class="w-full h-full object-cover"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro Bio Card Below Fold -->
  <main class="bg-white py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8 text-slate-700 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      
      <p class="text-center sm:text-left text-slate-800 text-xl font-medium">
        Over the last 15 years, I've hit some major life milestones—marriage, kids, property investments, relocation, even dealing with redundancy.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most financial media is written by suit-and-tie fund managers trying to sell complex products or keep you confused. I started Dad Investor to build the exact tools, calculators, and guides I wished I had when figuring out offset accounts, compounding ETF returns, and building long-term financial security for my family.
      </p>

      <!-- Key Principles Grid -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 pt-8">
        <div class="bg-[#0F291E] text-white p-8 rounded-3xl space-y-3 shadow-md">
          <span class="text-[#10B981] font-extrabold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">Principle 01</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">100% Plain English</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            No unnecessary Wall Street jargon. Just real math, clear numbers, and straightforward guidance for Aussie household budgets.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-100 p-8 rounded-3xl space-y-3 shadow-sm">
          <span class="text-emerald-800 font-extrabold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">Principle 02</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#0F291E]">Tools First, Opinions Second</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Interactive math helps you make your own informed financial decisions with your own family's numbers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
       <p>
        Most financial media is written by suit-and-tie fund managers trying to sell complex products or keep you confused. I started Dad Investor to build the exact tools, calculators, and guides I wished I had when figuring out offset accounts, compounding ETF returns, and building long-term financial security for my family.
      </p>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>